# GROMACS-style energy.xvg output - synthetic, matches the upstream
# plain-text whitespace-separated format. The wrapper parses the
# requested column (default column 1 = potential energy) and skips
# lines starting with '#' or '@'.
#
# Reference values: PE drifting between -345.7 and -340.1 across
# a 5-step sample. This is in the physically reasonable window for
# a small solvated peptide (Amber or CHARMM force field at 300 K).
# A wrapper that picks up column 2 instead of column 1 would read
# 425.0 - a value that fails our parse-window assertion.
@   title "GROMACS energy file"
@   xaxis  label "Time (ps)"
@   yaxis  label "Energy (kJ/mol)"
#
   0.000   425.0   -340.1
   0.002   425.5   -341.9
   0.004   426.0   -343.4
   0.006   425.7   -344.2
   0.008   425.3   -345.7
